{
  "case_id": "m1",
  "primary_mechanism": "Outer finalizer executes after dispatch early returns and after caught errors.",
  "source_truth": [
    "Health response is returned from dispatch, then gets header in fetch.",
    "Authentication failure returns 401 from dispatch, then gets header in fetch.",
    "Auth check precedes request.json and BUCKET.put.",
    "Parse/storage rejection is awaited and caught; generic 500 then gets header."
  ],
  "material_false_claim_traps": [
    "A return inside dispatch bypasses the caller header setter.",
    "The catch is unable to see asynchronous dispatch failures despite await.",
    "Malformed unauthorized JSON is parsed before authentication."
  ],
  "valid_remedies_or_limits": [
    "No demonstrated header coverage/order fix is required here. Optional input limits can be suggested without alleging absent header coverage."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        3,
        9
      ],
      "text": "  if (path === \"/health\") return new Response(\"ok\");\n  if (path !== \"/upload\") return new Response(\"Not found\", { status: 404 });\n  if (request.headers.get(\"Authorization\") !== `Bearer ${env.WRITE_KEY}`) {\n    return new Response(\"Unauthorized\", { status: 401 });\n  }\n  const body = await request.json();\n  await env.BUCKET.put(\"current\", JSON.stringify(body));"
    },
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        14,
        21
      ],
      "text": "    let response;\n    try {\n      response = await dispatch(request, env);\n    } catch (error) {\n      response = new Response(\"Internal error\", { status: 500 });\n    }\n    response.headers.set(\"X-Content-Type-Options\", \"nosniff\");\n    return response;"
    },
    {
      "file": "README.md",
      "lines": [
        2,
        2
      ],
      "text": "All responses, including health, authentication failures, missing routes, malformed JSON and storage errors, must include X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff. BUCKET is an R2 bucket. WRITE_KEY is always configured and secret. Authentication must precede parsing or storing uploads. Public health checks are intentional. All route implementation is in worker.js. A generic 500 for unexpected errors is acceptable for this service."
    }
  ]
}

