{
  "case_id": "c1",
  "primary_mechanism": "Queue callback awaits delivery; explicit ack/retry belongs to the message and survives handler success.",
  "source_truth": [
    "Callback uses awaited sequential for-of.",
    "Successful delivery is acknowledged after fetch completion and body consumption.",
    "Network error, response-read error or non-2xx causes message.retry().",
    "Explicit retry is not overridden by successful return of queue callback."
  ],
  "material_false_claim_traps": [
    "All caught failures are silently acknowledged because queue callback resolves.",
    "for-of with await behaves like discarded async forEach.",
    "Existing callback defines ctx or a Hono c binding."
  ],
  "valid_remedies_or_limits": [
    "Current ack/retry flow satisfies the stated delivery contract under given deduplication assumption. Awaited Promise.all with per-message retry handling could be an optional throughput change."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        7,
        9
      ],
      "text": "  const ok = response.ok;\n  await response.arrayBuffer();\n  if (!ok) throw new Error(\"Delivery failed\");"
    },
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        12,
        21
      ],
      "text": "  async queue(batch, env) {\n    for (const message of batch.messages) {\n      try {\n        await deliver(message, env);\n        message.ack();\n      } catch (error) {\n        message.retry();\n      }\n    }\n  }"
    },
    {
      "file": "reference.md",
      "lines": [
        18,
        18
      ],
      "text": "- If you call either `ack()` or `retry()` on a single message, and then either/any of `ackAll()` or `retryAll()` on the batch, the call on the single message takes precedence. That is, the batch-level call does not apply to that message (or messages, if multiple calls were made)."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "case_id": "c2",
  "primary_mechanism": "Discarded async forEach callbacks let queue handler finish without awaiting delivery; swallowed failure requests no retry.",
  "source_truth": [
    "forEach does not aggregate or await returned callback promises.",
    "Handler can resolve while external delivery remains pending, allowing successful-consumer acknowledgement before delivery finishes.",
    "Failure catch only logs; it calls neither retry nor throw.",
    "The shown parameters are batch and env; ctx and c are undefined identifiers in this module."
  ],
  "material_false_claim_traps": [
    "The async modifier on queue automatically awaits all async forEach callbacks.",
    "console.error triggers queue retry.",
    "A proposed replacement using ctx.waitUntil as shown is valid without adding or threading a ctx binding.",
    "HTTP response-return advice alone repairs this queue callback."
  ],
  "valid_remedies_or_limits": [
    "Replace forEach with an awaited for-of loop, ack after successful deliver, retry in catch (c1 is one valid shape).",
    "An awaited Promise.all over mapped tasks with correct per-message outcomes can also work. Do not require one wording or ban a properly scoped additional ctx parameter as a principle."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        12,
        21
      ],
      "text": "  async queue(batch, env) {\n    batch.messages.forEach(async (message) => {\n      try {\n        await deliver(message, env);\n        message.ack();\n      } catch (error) {\n        console.error(\"Delivery failed\", error);\n      }\n    });\n  }"
    },
    {
      "file": "reference.md",
      "lines": [
        12,
        12
      ],
      "text": "You can also acknowledge or negatively acknowledge messages at a batch level with `ackAll()` and `retryAll()`. Calling `ackAll()` on the batch of messages (`MessageBatch`) delivered to your consumer Worker has the same behaviour as a consumer Worker that successfully returns (does not throw an error)."
    },
    {
      "file": "README.md",
      "lines": [
        2,
        2
      ],
      "text": "This is a Queue consumer only. Delivery URL is a fixed trusted HTTPS target and is configured. Each body contains an eventId; the destination deduplicates by that eventId, so redelivery is safe. Every message must either complete delivery or request retry on delivery failure. Transient network errors and non-2xx responses happen in normal use. No hidden middleware, framework context or imports exist. The callback parameters shown are the only local bindings. Deploy configuration already connects the consumer and DLQ; changes to those are outside this review. reference.md is frozen documentation for this task."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "case_id": "p1",
  "primary_mechanism": "Explicit public-read/manual-capability policy is compatible with expiry and owner enforcement.",
  "source_truth": [
    "GET objects intentionally lacks auth and content is public.",
    "GET mint returns a proposal but never writes CAPS; operator insertion activates it.",
    "PUT requires existing CAPS record, rejects expiresAt <= now, and rejects owner mismatch before put.",
    "Expiry is enforced in code even if KV record has no native TTL.",
    "Same-key writes are serialized by explicit upstream lock, so a hypothetical overlapping HEAD/PUT ownership race contradicts fixture context."
  ],
  "material_false_claim_traps": [
    "Unauthenticated mint automatically produces active upload authority.",
    "Public object reads are an authentication bypass against the stated contract.",
    "Any subject can overwrite another subject in this exact snapshot.",
    "No native KV TTL means explicit expiresAt comparison cannot expire capabilities."
  ],
  "valid_remedies_or_limits": [
    "No demonstrated policy/expiry/ownership defect. Mint rate limiting or operational changes may be optional suggestions, not proofs of upload bypass."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "text": "    if (request.method === \"GET\" && path === \"/mint\") {\n      return Response.json({ token: crypto.randomUUID(), record: { sub: \"operator-selects-subject\", expiresAt: Date.now() + 3600000 } });"
    },
    {
      "file": "worker.js",
      "lines": [
        10,
        22
      ],
      "text": "    if (request.method === \"GET\") {\n      const object = await env.BUCKET.get(key);\n      return object ? new Response(object.body, { headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"text/plain\" } }) : new Response(\"Not found\", { status: 404 });\n    }\n    if (request.method !== \"PUT\") return new Response(\"Method not allowed\", { status: 405 });\n    const authorization = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\") || \"\";\n    const token = authorization.startsWith(\"Bearer \") ? authorization.slice(7) : \"\";\n    const capability = token ? await env.CAPS.get(token, \"json\") : null;\n    if (!capability) return new Response(\"Unauthorized\", { status: 401 });\n    if (Date.now() >= capability.expiresAt) return new Response(\"Expired\", { status: 401 });\n    const existing = await env.BUCKET.head(key);\n    if (existing && existing.customMetadata.owner !== capability.sub) return new Response(\"Forbidden\", { status: 403 });\n    await env.BUCKET.put(key, request.body, { customMetadata: { owner: capability.sub }, httpMetadata: { contentType: \"text/plain\" } });"
    },
    {
      "file": "README.md",
      "lines": [
        3,
        3
      ],
      "text": "GET /mint only proposes a random token and record. Operators review proposals out of band, choose a real subject and finite future expiresAt, and manually insert approved records into CAPS (a Workers KV namespace); the Worker never activates its proposals. Possessing a proposal alone grants no write access. All records in CAPS have a nonempty string sub and finite numeric expiresAt. Stale KV state after manual revocation is an accepted documented operational limitation, not a guarantee of immediate revocation."
    },
    {
      "file": "README.md",
      "lines": [
        5,
        5
      ],
      "text": "An upstream per-object lock serializes all PUT invocations to the same key through completion; same-key writes cannot overlap. This lock provides no authentication or owner check."
    }
  ]
}

